- Multiple threads take turns executing on a single\-core CPU; this is concurrency, but not parallelism in the strict sense;
- Multiple threads compute simultaneously on a multi\-core CPU; this is concurrency, and may also be parallelism;
- Using coroutines within a single thread to handle multiple network requests is concurrency, but does not necessarily involve multiple threads;
- C++ Parallel algorithms may use thread pools or other execution mechanisms, but users do not necessarily manage threads directly\.
